{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The focused tests pass, including the regression for a dirty base. I found two path-selection risks that can carry stale results: cross-module renames can omit the source module, and Git-quoted filenames can be treated as out-of-module changes. I’m tracing how those cases interact with the new self-contained exemption.\n\nThe sandbox refuses scratch-directory creation, so I can’t safely run the assessments that persist output. Both required validation commands have been invoked; neither has returned yet.\n"}}
