{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nFour blockers remain:\n\n- **N1 — high:** [validate_carry.go:107](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go#L107) relies on `git diff --name-only`, which omits a rename’s source path. Moving `a/required.txt` to `b/required.txt` can select only `b` and carry `a`’s old pass despite its required file disappearing. Include both rename endpoints and test this sequence.\n- **N2 — high:** [validate_scope.go:135](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go#L135) exempts self-contained modules after ownership matching fails. A root module `\".\"` never matches ordinary paths such as `main.go`, so its own changes can be carried. Handle root-module ownership explicitly.\n- **N3 — high:** [validate_scope.go:83](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go#L83) parses Git’s quoted, newline-delimited filenames as literal paths. A changed filename containing non-ASCII characters, quotes or newlines can lose its module ownership; the new self-contained exemption then carries that affected module. Use NUL-delimited path parsing.\n- **N4 — medium:** [validate_carry.go:184](pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go#L184) gives different dirty builds at the same revision the identical `<version>+<revision>.dirty` identity. Eligibility can therefore carry results across engine changes, contradicting D2. Reject unverifiable dirty engine identities or bind them to their actual build content.\n\nThese findings follow from code inspection; new reproduction fixtures could not be created because scratch storage is read-only.\n\nPrior **R1-F1 is fixed**: the dirty-base regression passes. Focused carry, selection, delivery/material-binding tests, focused race tests, and `go vet` passed. The module validation failed on sandbox write restrictions. Global validation reached 181 passes before cancellation. The supplied sealed matrix passes, but my required-tool runs did not establish a fresh passing gate.\n\nRules applied: review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. Reviewed bundle `rvb-b0296611766ddddc`; the design assessment reproduced sealed digest `design-b9c442f12ae40005`. No files changed or attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 107,\n      \"summary\": \"Carry selection inherits git diff --name-only's omission of rename source paths. Moving a required file from module a to module b can select only b and carry a's old pass after its input disappeared. Include both rename endpoints and add a regression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 135,\n      \"summary\": \"A selfContained root module '.' is skipped for its own changed files: moduleOf matches only '.' or './...' while Git returns paths such as main.go. Handle root-module ownership explicitly and test both carry and changed-from.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 83,\n      \"summary\": \"Quoted newline-delimited Git output is treated as literal paths. Changes to filenames containing non-ASCII characters, quotes or newlines can fail module ownership matching and then be excluded by selfContained, carrying stale results. Parse NUL-delimited paths and cover these filenames.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N4\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 184,\n      \"summary\": \"Different dirty engine builds at the same VCS revision receive the same version+revision.dirty identity and remain comparable. This permits carry across engine changes contrary to D2. Reject unverifiable dirty identities or bind eligibility to actual build content.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:93-99 rejects bases without material_clean or with unavailable bindings. TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy passed in the independent focused test run.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete implementation and documentation diff, R1-R10, D1-D3, ADR, carry eligibility, selection and exclusions, worker dispatch, result accounting, chained origins, delivery parsing, material freshness consumers, engine identity, legacy compatibility and existing regression coverage. Repository remained unchanged.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N4\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Explicit selfContained and declared-dependency assumptions are documented. Dirty-base eligibility is now verified, but engine identity does not establish unchanged engine content; path-selection findings also invalidate D1's unchanged-input premise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected silent carried-entry exclusion from dispatch, serial result accounting and cancellation handling. Focused carry/selection race tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive JSON fields, explicit flag restrictions and legacy parser fallback. Existing records retain their interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Flag refusals and revision confinement are conservative, but encoded Git path inputs can silently narrow validation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Delivery parsing preserves carried origins but attaches current run provenance; unsafe selection can consequently make stale carried outcomes current.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected fallback reasons, selected-module explanations, original observation fields and carried outcome accounting. Focused fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive CLI and file contracts, optional fields, legacy delivery reading and refusal of old bases without engine_version. No MCP signature changes were introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing positive and negative fixtures pass, but a self-contained root module can carry results after changes to its own inputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module reuse addresses repeated full validation, but D1 requires complete change selection. Rename-source omission breaks that causal guarantee.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records original-head reuse and the unchanged-input premise; D2 and D3 provide matrix/engine comparison and self-containment policy.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English and Portuguese manuals, embedded scaffold copies, help, spec and ADR. They consistently document flags, eligibility, provenance and declaration risks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected actionable canonical-path refusals, full-run fallback reasons and explain output. Existing diagnostic fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R6 requires a self-contained module to remain selected for its own changes; the root-module case violates that requirement. N1 and N3 additionally undermine R3 and D1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b9c442f12ae40005\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared changed implementation, tests, ADR, help and manuals against the spec's affected areas and artifact declarations. The implementation stays within the approved feature scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision option confinement and output-path restrictions remain intact, but incomplete selection permits stale evidence to acquire current material provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b9c442f12ae40005\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection and comparing the entire matrix is smaller than introducing per-check manifests or output caching. No speculative infrastructure was added. This choice remains sufficient only with complete path selection and trustworthy engine identity; the blockers identify those missing conditions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The first invocation completed and reported 14 claims, 19 observations and 985 findings; a clean strict result was not established. Its range ended at c1f54d56, whose differences from the checkout were verified to be only three derived index files. A second invocation intended to capture the standalone exit status was cancelled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b9c442f12ae40005\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the requested command; its input digest and ADR delta match the sealed structural evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This assessment persists output. Scratch-directory creation was refused, and the sealed checkout must remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This assessment persists output. Writable scratch was unavailable. Inspected the result producer, delivery parser and freshness consumers directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This assessment persists output. Writable scratch was unavailable; no assessment publication was attempted in the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the